\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s10 \li1209 \fi-1007 \ri1007 \ql Class Description \
\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 NSDecimalNumber, an immutable subclass of NSNumber, provides an object-oriented wrapper for doing base-10 arithmetic. An instance can represent any number that can be expressed as \i mantissa\i0 \'80\b x\b0 \'8010\f0 \b \fs24 exponent\f1 \b0 \i \fs28  \i0 where \i mantissa\i0  is a decimal integer up to 38 digits long, and \i exponent\i0  is an integer between -128 and 127.\
\fs14\
\fs28 In the course of doing arithmetic, a method may produce calculation errors, such as division by zero. It may also meet circumstances where it has a choice of ways to round a number off. The way the method acts on such occasions is called its \'aabehavior.\'ba \
\fs14\
\fs28 Behavior is set by methods in the NSDecimalNumberBehaviors protocol. Every NSDecimalNumber argument called \i behavior\i0  requires an object that conforms to this protocol. For more on behaviors, see the specifications for the NSDecimalNumberBehaviors protocol and the NSDecimalNumberHandler class. Also see the \b defaultBehavior\b0  method description, below.\
\fs14\
\fs26\
\f0 \b \fs28 \pard \s59 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql C Interface to Decimal Numbers\
\fs8\
\fs6\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 The arithmetic and rounding methods of NSDecimalNumber are also accessible through group of ordinary C functions, defined in NSDecimal.h. You might consider the C interface if you don\'27t need to treat NSDecimalNumbers as objects\'d0that is, if you don\'27t need to store them in an object-oriented collection like an NSArray or NSDictionary.\
\fs14\
\fs28 You might also consider the C interface if you need maximum efficiency. The C interface is faster and uses less memory than the NSDecimalNumberClass.\
\fs14\
\fs28 If you need mutability, you can combine the two interfaces. Use functions from the C interface and convert their results to NSDecimalNumbers.\
\fs14\
\fs28 The C functions\'d0\b NSDecimalCompact()\b0 , \b NSDecimalCompare()\b0 , \b NSDecimalRound()\b0 , \b NSDecimalNormalize()\b0 , \b NSDecimalAdd()\b0 , \b NSDecimalSubtract()\b0 , \b NSDecimalMultiply()\b0 , \b NSDecimalDivide()\b0 , \b NSDecimalPower()\b0 , \b NSDecimalMultiplyByPowerOf10()\b0 , \b NSDecimalString()\b0 \'d0are all documented in the \'aaFunctions\'ba chapter of the \i Foundation Framework Reference\i0 .\
\fs14\
