\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Creates and returns an NSDecimalNumber equivalent to \i numericString.\i0  Besides digits, \i numericString\i0  can include an initial \'aa+\'ba or \'aa-,\'ba a single \'aaE\'ba or \'aae\'ba, to indicate the exponent of a number in scientific notation, and a single NSDecimalSeparator to divide the fractional from the integral part of the number.\
\fs14\
\fs28 Whether the NSDecimalSeparator is a period (as in the United States) or a comma (as in France) depends on the default locale.\
\fs14\
